WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.130
[ Watch on KissFlix.co ]

2
00:05.400 --> 00:06.401
[This drama is intended for entertainment purposes only.]

3
00:06.411 --> 00:08.400
[All characters, behaviors, locations, and events depicted are fictional.]

4
00:08.430 --> 00:09.950
[It is not intended to be sexually suggestive or to encourage viewers]

5
00:10.000 --> 00:11.501
[to engage in inappropriate or morally objectionable behavior.]

6
00:11.511 --> 00:12.890
[Nor is it intended to discredit any profession]

7
00:12.899 --> 00:13.900
[or create negative perceptions of any organization]

8
00:13.911 --> 00:14.912
[or any particular group of people.]

9
00:14.976 --> 00:18.840
We've already issued an invitation to bid through e-bidding.

10
00:19.083 --> 00:21.600
We haven't made the terms of reference too restrictive,

11
00:21.627 --> 00:24.840
because we want to give young entrepreneurs and smaller companies

12
00:24.901 --> 00:26.702
a chance to submit their bids too.

13
00:26.750 --> 00:28.520
Why don't we bid on her Smart Card project?

14
00:28.751 --> 00:30.752
Government contracts require deep pockets

15
00:30.856 --> 00:31.857
because payments take forever.

16
00:32.011 --> 00:35.120
A small company like ours doesn't stand a chance.

17
00:35.243 --> 00:36.560
I'm here to see the Minister.

18
00:36.700 --> 00:39.720
I've agreed to take the money and stay away from the Director.

19
00:39.744 --> 00:40.745
Ten million.

20
00:40.795 --> 00:42.170
And how can I be sure

21
00:43.526 --> 00:44.960
that once you get the money,

22
00:45.792 --> 00:47.400
you'll really leave my husband alone?

23
00:47.483 --> 00:48.840
I'm a woman of my word.

24
00:49.270 --> 00:51.480
Have you talked to Ta lately?

25
00:51.494 --> 00:53.040
Why do you ask, Uncle Phop?

26
00:53.259 --> 00:56.590
She suddenly blocked me on everything.

27
00:56.608 --> 00:58.880
She didn't even tell me why. I don't know what's wrong.

28
00:59.083 --> 01:01.480
Ma'am, that bitch Mutta sent you a package.

29
01:01.627 --> 01:03.220
- What is that? - It's money.

30
01:03.240 --> 01:04.480
There must be millions in here.

31
01:05.400 --> 01:08.101
Our informant just sent us these photos. This just happened.

32
01:08.736 --> 01:09.920
Mutta! You bitch!

33
01:13.360 --> 01:14.880
[Foster Home]

34
01:16.774 --> 01:17.775
What are your names, dears?

35
01:20.865 --> 01:22.800
Answer when an adult asks you a question.

36
01:24.226 --> 01:27.160
I'm Munin. This is Mutta.

37
01:28.850 --> 01:29.851
"Yes, ma'am."

38
01:30.130 --> 01:34.576
When an adult asks you something, you must answer politely.

39
01:34.747 --> 01:36.760
Always say "yes, ma'am" or "yes, sir." Understand?

40
01:37.334 --> 01:38.335
Yes, ma'am.

41
01:39.700 --> 01:42.520
From now on, you two will start a new life here.

42
01:43.142 --> 01:45.880
You'll make new friends and follow new rules.

43
01:46.646 --> 01:50.160
And I'll be your new mother here.

44
01:52.374 --> 01:54.175
What about our mother?

45
01:54.800 --> 01:57.600
Will she come here too... ma'am?

46
01:58.576 --> 01:59.577
No, dear.

47
02:00.331 --> 02:01.332
You don't have to worry about that.

48
02:01.558 --> 02:05.440
She'll never be able to hurt you again.

49
02:07.771 --> 02:10.920
Take the two girls to bathe and get changed.

50
02:10.997 --> 02:13.000
Then show them where they'll be sleeping.

51
02:21.046 --> 02:24.360
Mutta, we won't have to see Mom again. Aren't you happy?

52
02:24.798 --> 02:25.799
Yeah.

53
02:27.915 --> 02:31.000
When will the twins' mother be released?

54
02:32.992 --> 02:34.700
The court sentenced her to life in prison.

55
03:57.014 --> 03:58.015
Mutta,

56
03:58.150 --> 04:01.120
if you're around, please guide me.

57
04:01.744 --> 04:02.891
Help me make the right choice.

58
04:03.654 --> 04:04.680
I can't afford to get this wrong.

59
04:10.408 --> 04:11.800
I'm betting ten million on one go.

60
04:12.424 --> 04:14.640
If I win, I'll get a hundred million back.

61
04:14.883 --> 04:17.180
But if I lose, I'll lose everything.

62
04:18.918 --> 04:20.440
Will I finally get my revenge?

63
04:21.072 --> 04:22.760
It all comes down to this one click.

64
04:42.771 --> 04:44.568
Why are you calling? To make up with me?

65
04:45.150 --> 04:46.350
I'm busy. Bye.

66
04:46.563 --> 04:47.960
I'm not calling to make up.

67
04:48.606 --> 04:51.700
I just wanted to ask if you've broken up with Uncle Phop.

68
04:52.728 --> 04:54.947
Why? Happy to hear that?

69
04:55.822 --> 04:58.600
If it's true, of course I am. I can keep pursuing you.

70
04:59.800 --> 05:00.801
Veekit,

71
05:01.182 --> 05:03.680
you need to stop trying to claim me after your uncle.

72
05:04.216 --> 05:05.440
I've told you before, haven't I?

73
05:05.651 --> 05:07.960
I'm not the same sweet, innocent Mutta anymore.

74
05:08.419 --> 05:09.800
That's exactly why

75
05:10.680 --> 05:12.250
I like you even more now.

76
05:20.440 --> 05:23.224
It's rare to see Phop staying home for once.

77
05:24.000 --> 05:25.720
Normally, on holidays like this,

78
05:26.046 --> 05:28.590
he'd be traveling somewhere, either here or abroad.

79
05:29.251 --> 05:30.640
I wonder what's gotten into him.

80
05:35.900 --> 05:37.280
- Na. - Yes?

81
05:37.379 --> 05:38.800
Go cleaning up outside for now.

82
05:39.000 --> 05:40.001
Yes, ma'am.

83
05:46.984 --> 05:48.720
I bought him back with money.

84
05:49.176 --> 05:51.520
If I'd known it was this easy, I'd have done it ages ago.

85
05:54.222 --> 05:55.440
You bought him back?

86
05:56.088 --> 05:57.700
What do you mean? From whom?

87
05:59.702 --> 06:02.080
I bought Phop back from that Mutta.

88
06:03.584 --> 06:06.160
I offered her a sum of money

89
06:06.262 --> 06:07.640
to stay away from Phop.

90
06:07.851 --> 06:11.240
At first, I thought I might just be throwing my money away.

91
06:11.620 --> 06:15.240
But believe it or not, even that whore has some decency.

92
06:15.414 --> 06:17.160
She actually agreed to leave him, Soi!

93
06:17.920 --> 06:18.921
Really?

94
06:19.440 --> 06:23.120
Thank goodness! Who knew it would be this easy?

95
06:23.587 --> 06:25.121
So how much did you pay that bitch?

96
06:25.680 --> 06:26.681
Ten million.

97
06:27.200 --> 06:28.280
Ten million?

98
06:30.736 --> 06:34.971
No wonder she agreed. I'd take the money too.

99
06:35.398 --> 06:37.760
Ten million in exchange for one useless man?

100
06:38.056 --> 06:39.720
Who'd be stupid enough to choose the man?

101
06:43.150 --> 06:46.680
But it was worth it to get your husband back.

102
06:46.914 --> 06:49.134
Your children have their father back, too.

103
06:49.342 --> 06:52.760
And your family is whole and happy again.

104
06:53.203 --> 06:56.792
Even twenty million would be a bargain, if you ask me.

105
07:02.275 --> 07:03.276
Hello?

106
07:03.624 --> 07:05.280
Have you seen the money I transferred?

107
07:05.795 --> 07:08.440
Yeah, I have. Why the hell did you send me fifty million?

108
07:09.142 --> 07:12.200
Didn't you say we needed deep pockets to get into government contracts?

109
07:12.630 --> 07:15.800
We're going to land the smart card project from the ministry.

110
07:16.267 --> 07:17.680
You can get started today.

111
07:18.171 --> 07:20.172
Where did you get all that money?

112
07:20.920 --> 07:22.021
Crypto trading.

113
07:23.464 --> 07:24.465
I've got to go.

114
07:29.200 --> 07:30.201
Director.

115
07:31.011 --> 07:33.358
Mutta, what kind of game are you playing with me now?

116
07:33.779 --> 07:36.280
One minute you're gone, the next you're back. I'm so confused.

117
07:37.219 --> 07:40.400
Keeping you guessing makes our love life more exciting.

118
07:41.220 --> 07:42.521
Let's have lunch together today.

119
07:54.723 --> 07:58.300
It's the latest iPhone. That's my phone.

120
07:58.643 --> 08:01.280
She broke her promise after all. That bitch!

121
08:03.502 --> 08:06.050
I don't have an appointment. May I still see him?

122
08:06.824 --> 08:08.974
Mutta, what the hell are you playing at?

123
08:09.494 --> 08:10.731
Ten million!

124
08:10.907 --> 08:14.960
A low-ranking civil servant like you couldn't earn that much in three lifetimes!

125
08:15.104 --> 08:16.520
Instead of holding on to it for dear life.

126
08:16.566 --> 08:17.700
What kind of game are you playing with me?

127
08:17.968 --> 08:19.520
I'm just following your advice, ma'am.

128
08:20.064 --> 08:23.090
You said smart people these days trade crypto.

129
08:23.296 --> 08:24.680
So I thought I'd give it a try.

130
08:24.992 --> 08:27.760
As luck would have it, I made a little profit.

131
08:27.926 --> 08:31.250
Enough to get by, so I thought I'd return your ten million.

132
08:31.550 --> 08:34.640
Thank you so much for showing me how to get rich.

133
08:34.968 --> 08:36.680
And for giving me the money to get started.

134
08:37.539 --> 08:38.540
I'm forever grateful.

135
08:40.043 --> 08:41.044
You bitch!

136
08:41.115 --> 08:42.240
Get out!

137
08:42.406 --> 08:44.200
- Get out! - Calm down, ma'am. Get a hold of yourself.

138
08:44.486 --> 08:45.487
Please calm down.

139
08:48.054 --> 08:49.320
Good for you, now that you're rich.

140
08:50.222 --> 08:51.640
So you'll leave my husband alone, right?

141
08:52.392 --> 08:55.120
Just so you know, Phop isn't rolling in money.

142
08:55.278 --> 08:56.400
It's all my money!

143
08:58.126 --> 08:59.400
Let me make one thing clear, ma'am.

144
09:00.547 --> 09:03.560
I'm not seeing the Director for his money.

145
09:03.950 --> 09:05.760
It's purely for the amazing sex.

146
09:06.200 --> 09:07.700
I've got a thing for a man like him.

147
09:08.147 --> 09:10.800
Why not share something this good?

148
09:11.235 --> 09:14.760
Once I'm done with him, I send him home for you to enjoy.

149
09:15.356 --> 09:17.157
It's not like he's going to wear out on me.

150
09:18.300 --> 09:19.301
Mutta, you bitch!

151
09:19.891 --> 09:22.720
I'll kill you!

152
09:27.987 --> 09:29.080
As if you haven't tried before.

153
09:30.291 --> 09:32.520
Too bad for you, I'm not that easy to kill.

154
09:32.862 --> 09:34.880
You made a huge mistake

155
09:35.187 --> 09:36.800
letting me live this long.

156
09:39.790 --> 09:42.600
What the hell are you talking about? When did I ever try to kill you?

157
09:44.440 --> 09:45.441
Do you have any proof?

158
09:45.827 --> 09:47.600
- Should we get you drug-tested? - Go ahead.

159
09:48.126 --> 09:51.160
But you might find traces of the Director's bodily fluids, too.

160
09:51.619 --> 09:53.080
We just finished having sex.

161
09:54.872 --> 09:55.773
You bitch!

162
09:55.779 --> 09:57.220
Please calm down, ma'am.

163
09:57.223 --> 09:58.660
- Let go of me! - Ma'am!

164
09:59.600 --> 10:00.601
Mutta, you bitch!

165
10:02.480 --> 10:05.400
Get this through your thick skull.

166
10:06.363 --> 10:07.960
As long as I'm alive,

167
10:08.608 --> 10:10.680
I'll devote every ounce of my energy

168
10:11.206 --> 10:12.720
to messing with your head.

169
10:13.579 --> 10:14.920
You won't get away from me.

170
10:15.995 --> 10:17.000
Mutta, you bitch!

171
10:17.195 --> 10:18.680
Mutta!

172
10:18.688 --> 10:20.200
Let go of me! I'll kill her!

173
10:20.240 --> 10:21.680
- I'll kill her! - Ma'am, please!

174
10:21.800 --> 10:23.720
- That bitch Mutta! - You can't, ma'am!

175
10:23.840 --> 10:26.640
The election is coming up. You can't kill anyone now!

176
10:26.736 --> 10:28.400
What's one more person?

177
10:29.100 --> 10:30.800
- Please calm down, ma'am! - Let go of me!

178
10:32.166 --> 10:33.167
Please sit down.

179
10:33.467 --> 10:34.468
Calm down, ma'am.

180
10:38.448 --> 10:40.480
Every political party is looking for a way to bring you down.

181
10:41.376 --> 10:42.480
Please be patient a little longer, ma'am.

182
10:43.243 --> 10:44.760
Once the election is over and your party forms the government,

183
10:45.147 --> 10:46.500
we can deal with her then.

184
10:57.654 --> 10:58.655
Jolene.

185
11:02.131 --> 11:03.132
What are you all doing?

186
11:04.160 --> 11:07.280
We just submitted our bid for the smart card project.

187
11:09.851 --> 11:11.560
Please let us win.

188
11:13.275 --> 11:15.880
Oh, Munin! Perfect timing. Come pray with us.

189
11:15.900 --> 11:17.320
Everyone else has already prayed. Come on.

190
11:17.600 --> 11:19.201
Let's go pray at the spirit house.

191
11:19.643 --> 11:21.440
Come on, hurry.

192
11:27.726 --> 11:29.955
Hey, take this seriously.

193
11:30.200 --> 11:32.120
If we win this contract,

194
11:32.254 --> 11:34.446
we'll be able to use it to pitch for other projects

195
11:34.550 --> 11:36.300
and walk in with our heads held high.

196
11:36.451 --> 11:37.452
Let me show you.

197
11:40.163 --> 11:43.640
Hello, I'm Jolene from Queen Byte,

198
11:43.774 --> 11:48.720
the company behind the smart card system used by over 70 million Thais.

199
11:50.275 --> 11:52.000
I'd love to get the credit,

200
11:52.627 --> 11:54.080
but what I want even more

201
11:54.995 --> 11:57.450
is to wreak havoc on that bitch Nopnapha's career.

202
11:57.952 --> 11:59.800
Just wait and see.

203
12:00.918 --> 12:02.600
I'll make her suffer like never before.

204
12:09.990 --> 12:11.400
It's from Mr. Thanong, ma'am.

205
12:12.811 --> 12:14.560
Deposit it in the Singapore bank as usual.

206
12:14.832 --> 12:16.520
But use a different account from last time.

207
12:17.078 --> 12:18.079
Yes, ma'am.

208
12:26.950 --> 12:29.718
Touch, I've gone through all the company profiles.

209
12:30.395 --> 12:32.360
Which company do you think looks the most promising?

210
12:32.728 --> 12:34.680
There are three or four promising companies.

211
12:35.240 --> 12:36.376
I've shortlisted them for you.

212
12:36.600 --> 12:39.601
One company's partner works in the US.

213
12:39.998 --> 12:41.400
They might have some new software

214
12:41.656 --> 12:42.960
that we could use, too.

215
12:43.307 --> 12:46.240
Yeah, I'm interested in that company as well.

216
12:49.920 --> 12:50.921
Just a second.

217
12:51.110 --> 12:53.758
Go play somewhere else. Mommy's busy.

218
12:53.886 --> 12:57.240
Mom, you forgot to tell Oshi to buy me the Bambinana Red Hat!

219
12:57.672 --> 12:59.040
Wait, what did you say?

220
12:59.534 --> 13:02.974
Bambinana! Bambinana!

221
13:03.478 --> 13:06.060
- Oshi! - Yes?

222
13:06.115 --> 13:07.520
- Come here for a second. - Yes, ma'am.

223
13:08.083 --> 13:11.520
What on earth is this Bamba-baba, Bibi-baba thing?

224
13:11.582 --> 13:13.520
Oh, it's an art toy, ma'am.

225
13:13.560 --> 13:16.440
It's what Titus asked you to get for her birthday.

226
13:18.043 --> 13:19.100
I must've forgotten.

227
13:19.120 --> 13:20.806
Go get one for her. How much does it cost?

228
13:20.821 --> 13:24.020
Oh, it's sold out, ma'am. It's a limited edition.

229
13:24.040 --> 13:26.300
It went on sale this morning, and fewer than a hundred were available.

230
13:26.726 --> 13:29.000
I've tried asking people who managed to buy one,

231
13:29.027 --> 13:30.800
but nobody's willing to resell theirs, ma'am.

232
13:31.862 --> 13:35.600
Titus, I'll buy you one when the next version comes out, okay?

233
13:35.620 --> 13:36.960
I promise I won't forget this time.

234
13:37.342 --> 13:40.131
- No! I want this one! - Titus!

235
13:40.227 --> 13:43.400
It's wearing a red hat! A red hat!

236
13:43.915 --> 13:46.656
- I want this one! I want this one! - Phop, come here!

237
13:46.784 --> 13:49.150
Hurry! Your son's throwing a tantrum!

238
13:49.211 --> 13:50.212
What's wrong?

239
13:50.312 --> 13:53.313
- It's got a red hat, Mom! I want this one! - What a headache!

240
13:53.400 --> 13:55.240
- Titus, sweetheart! Titus! - Wait, where were we?

241
13:55.250 --> 13:56.520
- What does Daddy's precious little girl want? - Go on.

242
13:56.982 --> 13:57.983
Okay.

243
13:58.144 --> 13:59.400
And don't forget, for this project,

244
13:59.450 --> 14:01.720
- We're only taking 15%. - What do you want?

245
14:01.899 --> 14:04.040
I want Bambinana!

246
14:04.120 --> 14:06.550
Hey, get down first! You'll hurt yourself!

247
14:06.800 --> 14:07.801
What do you want, sweetheart?

248
14:07.811 --> 14:10.812
I want the Bambinana Red Hat!

249
14:10.840 --> 14:12.720
The one wearing a red hat!

250
14:12.800 --> 14:15.301
Oh, how about Toi Red Hat instead, sweetie?

251
14:15.891 --> 14:17.400
Dad, what are you talking about?

252
14:20.456 --> 14:22.320
Excuse me, sir. That's a singer.

253
14:23.457 --> 14:24.458
I know that!

254
14:37.440 --> 14:38.520
Here you go, Mutta.

255
14:41.502 --> 14:44.680
What should we have for lunch? I'm sick of cafeteria food.

256
14:44.819 --> 14:46.720
How about Som Tam Je Pu outside the Ministry?

257
14:48.019 --> 14:50.120
Oh, let's go! Come on, get up!

258
14:51.200 --> 14:52.201
It's not even noon yet.

259
14:54.611 --> 14:56.360
If we wait until noon, we won't get to eat.

260
14:57.086 --> 14:58.840
You know how crowded that place gets.

261
14:59.870 --> 15:01.040
What about Toey?

262
15:01.400 --> 15:04.160
If he finds out, we'll all get scolded.

263
15:04.755 --> 15:06.360
Everyone else is still working.

264
15:07.142 --> 15:10.470
Hong, we'll just sneak out. He won't even know.

265
15:10.523 --> 15:13.124
Come on, we've done it plenty of times.

266
15:13.478 --> 15:17.400
Exactly. I don't think it's right.

267
15:17.640 --> 15:19.400
So, are you coming or not?

268
15:21.254 --> 15:22.255
I'm coming.

269
15:23.254 --> 15:24.255
- That's more like it! - There you go!

270
15:25.100 --> 15:26.262
Let's go, Mutta.

271
15:34.587 --> 15:37.280
We're just going out for lunch. Why all the sneaking around?

272
15:37.520 --> 15:39.600
Because it's not lunchtime yet, Mutta.

273
15:39.600 --> 15:41.680
Look, there's hardly anyone around.

274
15:45.467 --> 15:47.568
Hello, Director.

275
15:51.192 --> 15:52.193
Where are you all going?

276
15:52.800 --> 15:55.520
We're going for som tam outside the Ministry. Want to join us?

277
15:57.294 --> 15:59.160
Why don't you come have lunch with me instead? Let's go.

278
16:06.288 --> 16:08.240
I'll pretend I didn't notice

279
16:08.571 --> 16:10.680
that you all took your lunch break early.

280
16:12.326 --> 16:16.000
You can even come back a little late. I won't mind.

281
16:17.300 --> 16:18.301
But

282
16:19.787 --> 16:22.720
you mustn't gossip about me and Mutta having lunch together.

283
16:23.526 --> 16:25.894
Understood?

284
16:26.420 --> 16:28.800
Yes, Director.

285
16:47.040 --> 16:52.041
Oshi, Mutta just went out to lunch with the Director.

286
16:54.606 --> 16:58.240
On the day of the e-bidding, we'll rig it so they win.

287
16:59.326 --> 17:00.400
But don't worry.

288
17:00.510 --> 17:03.180
Our system is foolproof. No one will ever catch us.

289
17:13.611 --> 17:15.012
In my opinion,

290
17:15.584 --> 17:17.385
this will improve our image among the younger generation.

291
17:17.700 --> 17:19.601
We're giving startups a chance,

292
17:20.101 --> 17:22.602
which also aligns with our future policies.

293
17:32.651 --> 17:35.035
Are you sure your wife won't come after me?

294
17:35.800 --> 17:38.700
After what happened, she'll probably be keeping a close eye on you.

295
17:40.700 --> 17:41.701
She's too busy for that.

296
17:42.446 --> 17:44.880
She's caught up in some massive project of hers.

297
17:46.222 --> 17:47.640
You mean the smart card project?

298
17:50.155 --> 17:51.730
You're interested in that sort of thing, Mutta?

299
17:52.715 --> 17:54.350
I just happened to see it on the news.

300
18:01.766 --> 18:02.767
Cheers!

301
18:10.472 --> 18:11.473
Mutta,

302
18:12.152 --> 18:15.400
do you know that doll called Babina-Babini or something?

303
18:16.766 --> 18:19.120
- Bambinana? - Yeah, that's the one!

304
18:20.040 --> 18:22.360
My daughter really wants one.

305
18:22.766 --> 18:24.480
But the limited edition is sold out.

306
18:24.787 --> 18:26.680
It's driving me crazy. I have no idea where to find one.

307
18:27.326 --> 18:29.600
Do you know where I could buy one?

308
18:31.736 --> 18:33.807
Once a limited edition sells out, that's it.

309
18:34.824 --> 18:37.300
It could take years before someone resells one.

310
18:38.040 --> 18:39.080
Years?

311
18:41.752 --> 18:43.520
My daughter threw a tantrum all night.

312
18:43.867 --> 18:46.700
She said we didn't love her because we couldn't buy her that toy.

313
18:48.075 --> 18:50.000
Being a parent is tough.

314
18:50.342 --> 18:52.280
If I could turn back time, I wouldn't have had her.

315
18:56.343 --> 18:59.300
By the way, have you gotten your contraceptive implant yet?

316
19:01.600 --> 19:02.601
Yes, I have.

317
19:03.232 --> 19:04.233
Really?

318
19:04.900 --> 19:05.901
That's great!

319
19:05.947 --> 19:09.000
After we finish eating, let's go have some fun.

320
19:09.846 --> 19:13.360
Ever since you came back, I haven't gotten any action from you.

321
19:14.734 --> 19:16.700
- Maybe another day. - No way!

322
19:17.843 --> 19:19.600
I'm not letting you put me off anymore.

323
19:20.800 --> 19:22.320
Even if there's a red light,

324
19:23.128 --> 19:24.160
I'm going straight through it.

325
19:25.576 --> 19:27.440
I don't care how much the fine is.

326
20:09.390 --> 20:10.720
Wait, Director.

327
20:11.064 --> 20:13.320
Let's get a little tipsy first. It'll spice things up.

328
20:16.387 --> 20:18.880
Sure! I'll make it extra spicy for you.

329
20:20.062 --> 20:21.063
Bottoms up!

330
20:36.702 --> 20:38.300
Director! Director!

331
20:38.526 --> 20:40.727
You're the best, Director!

332
20:41.043 --> 20:42.560
Director? More like Dynamite in Bed!

333
20:42.792 --> 20:45.280
Director! Oh, Director!

334
20:46.600 --> 20:47.601
Director!

335
21:00.518 --> 21:02.600
Director! Director!

336
21:42.088 --> 21:43.089
Mutta.

337
21:43.822 --> 21:44.823
What happened?

338
21:46.211 --> 21:49.780
You thrust so hard you nearly broke my pelvis,

339
21:50.072 --> 21:51.360
and now you're asking what happened?

340
21:55.110 --> 21:56.111
Huh?

341
21:56.550 --> 21:57.651
Wait, we already had sex?

342
21:59.504 --> 22:00.560
It's almost four o'clock.

343
22:00.752 --> 22:03.440
Hurry back to work. It's almost time to clock out.

344
22:13.880 --> 22:14.881
How the hell is that possible?

345
22:42.609 --> 22:44.320
Hey, baby. What's up?

346
22:44.592 --> 22:47.240
Babe, sorry for waking you up in the middle of the night.

347
22:47.659 --> 22:50.080
I need a huge favor.

348
22:50.400 --> 22:53.300
I want a Bambinana doll with a red hat.

349
22:53.500 --> 22:55.440
It's only sold at the store in Vegas.

350
22:55.501 --> 22:58.300
Do you have any friends in Vegas who could get one for me?

351
22:58.700 --> 22:59.920
Friends in Vegas?

352
23:01.800 --> 23:04.001
No. Why don't you just buy it online?

353
23:04.801 --> 23:07.920
It's a limited edition, only available in-store.

354
23:08.894 --> 23:11.640
How about this, babe? Could you drive there and get one for me?

355
23:12.318 --> 23:14.760
Sure, I'll take care of it this weekend.

356
23:15.550 --> 23:17.960
You have to go tonight! It goes on sale at 10 a.m.

357
23:18.232 --> 23:20.180
And you'll have to line up. There are only a few available.

358
23:20.478 --> 23:21.520
At three in the morning?

359
23:22.355 --> 23:23.640
You want me to go buy a toy right now?

360
23:24.451 --> 23:26.760
If you drive from here to Vegas, you'll get there by morning.

361
23:27.064 --> 23:28.760
Please, babe?

362
23:29.230 --> 23:30.231
I'm begging you.

363
23:31.827 --> 23:33.880
Hmm. I'll take care of it…

364
23:34.328 --> 23:35.329
as always.

365
23:39.400 --> 23:41.401
[Bangkok Remand Prison, 125th Anniversary]

366
23:53.366 --> 23:54.367
Aren't you going to eat?

367
23:55.702 --> 23:56.903
I'm sick of this dog food.

368
23:58.219 --> 23:59.840
I'm eating outside today.

369
24:00.578 --> 24:03.000
Keep talking big. You'll starve to death.

370
24:06.700 --> 24:08.400
- Jintana. - Yes.

371
24:08.440 --> 24:09.840
- Jongsawat. - That's right.

372
24:12.272 --> 24:16.240
You've been granted a sentence reduction under the Royal Pardon Decree.

373
24:16.470 --> 24:19.840
Your recalculated sentence ends today.

374
24:20.152 --> 24:21.153
Prepare for release.

375
24:23.422 --> 24:24.423
Thank you.

376
24:25.784 --> 24:26.785
Bye-bye!

377
24:26.900 --> 24:27.901
Bye-bye!

378
24:33.179 --> 24:36.480
Do you think I've been too hard on Andrew, making him do all this stuff?

379
24:38.614 --> 24:42.320
A little, yeah. I actually feel sorry for your boyfriend.

380
24:42.700 --> 24:44.080
Look how he does everything you ask.

381
24:44.501 --> 24:46.300
But you barely seem to care about him.

382
24:46.800 --> 24:47.801
Of course I care!

383
24:48.432 --> 24:51.800
I just want that stupid banana doll to mess with Nopnapha.

384
24:52.422 --> 24:53.723
I've come up with a new plan.

385
24:54.406 --> 24:56.080
I'm going to use her daughter against her.

386
24:56.704 --> 24:59.259
What? You're dragging a child into this too?

387
24:59.931 --> 25:01.286
What are you planning to do to the poor girl?

388
25:07.648 --> 25:10.206
Hang on. It's my condo management calling.

389
25:13.110 --> 25:14.111
Hello?

390
25:16.100 --> 25:17.101
What?

391
25:18.701 --> 25:19.902
Are you sure there's no mistake?

392
25:21.600 --> 25:22.601
Okay, I'll come down.

393
25:23.900 --> 25:24.901
I've got to go. Talk later.

394
25:36.275 --> 25:38.200
Mutta! Mutta!

395
25:38.700 --> 25:40.360
Is that you, sweetheart? Mutta!

396
25:40.870 --> 25:43.240
I've missed you so much, my dear.

397
25:48.046 --> 25:50.640
Sorry, ma'am. You've got the wrong person.

398
25:51.320 --> 25:53.860
You bitch! Why didn't you say so sooner?

399
26:02.558 --> 26:04.520
Ugh, so annoying!

400
26:06.264 --> 26:09.800
What the hell are you crying for? What the hell?

401
26:10.856 --> 26:12.600
You're such a damn nuisance!

402
26:13.128 --> 26:14.440
Why are you crying?

403
26:15.848 --> 26:18.080
Look at me! I said stop!

404
26:18.640 --> 26:19.800
I said stop!

405
26:20.296 --> 26:22.080
I told you to stop! Why won't you stop, huh?

406
26:22.120 --> 26:24.160
Why won't you stop? Stop it already!

407
26:25.214 --> 26:26.680
Stop hitting your children, Jintana!

408
26:28.606 --> 26:31.080
You're under arrest for robbery and murder.

409
26:31.576 --> 26:32.867
You'll have to come with us for questioning.

410
26:32.968 --> 26:35.080
- Let's go! - I didn't do it! Don't arrest me!

411
26:35.720 --> 26:37.720
I was just trying to make money to feed my kids!

412
26:37.984 --> 26:39.800
I was just trying to provide for my kids!

413
26:39.897 --> 26:40.898
Take her to the police station.

414
26:47.898 --> 26:48.899
Mutta!

415
26:49.800 --> 26:50.801
Is that you, Mutta?

416
26:53.900 --> 26:54.901
It's Mom.

417
26:55.501 --> 26:58.440
You remember me, don't you, sweetheart? Don't you?

418
27:04.891 --> 27:06.250
This place is huge!

419
27:10.184 --> 27:11.930
How much did it cost? Ten million?

420
27:13.100 --> 27:14.920
I didn't buy it. I'm renting.

421
27:16.600 --> 27:18.501
I knew it!

422
27:18.570 --> 27:21.501
How could a lowly civil servant ever get rich?

423
27:23.166 --> 27:24.680
Why don't you try selling yourself?

424
27:24.700 --> 27:26.801
Put your youth and beauty to good use.

425
27:30.598 --> 27:31.728
Oh, and what about that bitch Munin?

426
27:32.096 --> 27:33.097
Where is she?

427
27:33.216 --> 27:34.360
I heard some foreigner adopted her

428
27:35.200 --> 27:37.920
from the foster home, right?

429
27:39.080 --> 27:40.081
Yeah.

430
27:40.440 --> 27:42.000
That bitch sure got lucky.

431
27:42.771 --> 27:45.200
I bet that foreigner took her as a wife.

432
27:46.830 --> 27:48.600
Has she ever contacted you?

433
27:51.500 --> 27:53.100
- No. - What an ungrateful bitch!

434
27:53.664 --> 27:55.920
She made it big and forgot all about her own sister.

435
27:57.201 --> 28:00.120
Forget about her, Mom. Just tell me why you're here.

436
28:00.750 --> 28:01.751
Why are you here?

437
28:03.542 --> 28:07.080
Does a mother need a reason to visit her own daughter?

438
28:07.400 --> 28:09.126
I missed you!

439
28:09.318 --> 28:10.880
Didn't you miss me at all?

440
28:11.771 --> 28:13.880
It's been over twenty years since we last saw each other.

441
28:16.696 --> 28:17.697
I...

442
28:18.664 --> 28:20.600
I never thought I'd see you again.

443
28:20.872 --> 28:22.340
They told me you were sentenced to life in prison.

444
28:23.443 --> 28:27.200
Nobody stays in prison for life. Everyone gets their sentence reduced.

445
28:29.544 --> 28:33.640
But while I was in prison, I missed you two so much.

446
28:34.488 --> 28:37.760
I counted down the days until I could see my daughters again.

447
28:38.787 --> 28:40.979
Mom, just get to the point.

448
28:43.000 --> 28:44.001
What do you want?

449
28:46.700 --> 28:48.400
Do you have some money you could give me?

450
28:48.742 --> 28:51.100
I want to use it to start a new life with my boyfriend.

451
28:55.043 --> 28:57.640
Forty-eight... forty-nine... fifty.

452
28:59.619 --> 29:02.686
That's my girl. I raised you right.

453
29:03.038 --> 29:04.766
I'll use this money to buy a phone.

454
29:04.840 --> 29:08.241
Then we can call each other whenever we miss each other.

455
29:08.700 --> 29:09.701
There's no need.

456
29:10.000 --> 29:11.801
Go start a new family with your boyfriend, Mom.

457
29:11.998 --> 29:13.520
And let's stay out of each other's lives.

458
29:14.899 --> 29:16.320
How can you be so heartless?

459
29:18.369 --> 29:21.072
A mother and daughter can never truly cut ties.

460
29:22.100 --> 29:23.101
But...

461
29:23.574 --> 29:26.880
if you give me a monthly allowance,

462
29:26.890 --> 29:29.160
I might not miss you quite so much.

463
29:35.656 --> 29:37.320
Is this the car you called to pick me up?

464
29:39.100 --> 29:42.360
How fancy! I haven't ridden in an air-conditioned car in ages.

465
29:44.800 --> 29:46.401
Well, I'll be off now, Munin.

466
29:47.901 --> 29:48.902
Mutta.

467
29:49.736 --> 29:51.300
- Are you Mutta or Munin? - Just go, Mom.

468
30:24.480 --> 30:26.806
So, did you get it?

469
30:27.643 --> 30:28.980
Yeah, I got it.

470
30:32.251 --> 30:33.252
Thanks.

471
30:33.547 --> 30:35.131
Thank you so much. Love you.

472
30:39.843 --> 30:40.844
Hey!

473
30:41.347 --> 30:42.348
What happened?

474
30:42.654 --> 30:45.347
I got the toy for you, right?

475
30:45.655 --> 30:48.600
I was about to mail it, but then...

476
30:50.326 --> 30:51.327
as you can see.

477
30:54.038 --> 30:56.576
What did the doctor say? Is it serious?

478
30:57.360 --> 30:59.680
Just a broken leg. I'll be in a cast for two months.

479
31:03.147 --> 31:04.360
I'm sorry.

480
31:05.755 --> 31:07.880
I don't even know what to say, except...

481
31:09.339 --> 31:11.840
sorry and get well soon.

482
31:15.040 --> 31:16.440
Have you sent me the package yet?

483
31:20.341 --> 31:21.342
What?

484
31:21.694 --> 31:23.800
Your mom got out of prison and showed up at your place asking for money.

485
31:24.350 --> 31:27.240
And your boyfriend Andrew broke his leg in a car accident.

486
31:27.662 --> 31:31.160
Seriously, your life is one disaster after another.

487
31:31.200 --> 31:32.646
How does everything get so chaotic?

488
31:33.414 --> 31:34.640
I guess I'm just having a run of bad luck.

489
31:36.651 --> 31:38.950
I hope nothing else happens to give me a heart attack.

490
31:46.091 --> 31:47.120
What's wrong, Khwan?

491
31:47.750 --> 31:49.880
The smart card project e-bidding results are out.

492
31:50.560 --> 31:51.961
Wait! Don't open it yet!

493
31:52.539 --> 31:53.540
I need to brace myself.

494
31:56.624 --> 31:57.625
Okay, open it.

495
32:01.696 --> 32:05.800
We regret to inform you that your company was not selected.

496
32:06.032 --> 32:08.678
Thank you for your interest in participating in the bidding process.

497
32:08.790 --> 32:12.360
We hope you'll participate in our future projects.

498
32:21.966 --> 32:24.650
Looks like we're both having a run of bad luck lately.

499
32:26.167 --> 32:28.568
It's okay. We can wait for the next project.

500
32:29.347 --> 32:30.840
I'm not upset about losing the contract.

501
32:31.734 --> 32:33.920
I'm upset that I missed my chance to get revenge on that bitch Nopnapha.

502
32:40.535 --> 32:41.536
Hey,

503
32:42.246 --> 32:45.051
can we find out which company won the bid?

504
32:58.800 --> 32:59.801
Wow.

505
33:00.500 --> 33:03.360
Your credentials are seriously impressive.

506
33:05.142 --> 33:07.143
It's such a shame, though.

507
33:08.374 --> 33:10.575
My company isn't hiring anyone right now.

508
33:13.635 --> 33:17.560
I saw that your company won the smart card project bid.

509
33:18.243 --> 33:20.400
So I'd love to put my experience to good use

510
33:20.920 --> 33:22.480
and help develop our country.

511
33:24.081 --> 33:25.600
I'd even be willing to work without pay.

512
33:28.082 --> 33:29.083
Please?

513
33:30.712 --> 33:32.300
Just give me a chance to work with you.

514
33:38.928 --> 33:40.840
I'll arrange a private office for you.

515
33:42.176 --> 33:44.043
That way, I can train you...

516
33:45.371 --> 33:46.372
without any interruptions.

517
33:47.867 --> 33:48.868
First things first,

518
33:49.942 --> 33:51.640
we need to turn on the computer.

519
33:53.382 --> 33:56.820
I'd like to start by reviewing all the company's information.

520
33:57.915 --> 33:59.016
We can discuss everything else later.

521
34:16.500 --> 34:17.501
Call me when you're done.

522
34:59.811 --> 35:01.360
Isn't Mutta joining us for lunch today?

523
35:03.422 --> 35:05.320
She called in sick today.

524
35:05.811 --> 35:09.080
I'm worried about her. I hope it's nothing serious.

525
35:12.500 --> 35:14.901
- Mind if I join you? - Of course, Veekit! Have a seat.

526
35:26.798 --> 35:27.799
Hello?

527
35:27.832 --> 35:30.160
Are you sick, Mutta? Is it serious?

528
35:32.600 --> 35:34.201
I've got a sore throat and a fever.

529
35:34.700 --> 35:36.780
I've already taken some medicine. I should be back at work tomorrow.

530
35:37.478 --> 35:40.160
Have you had lunch yet? Want me to bring you something?

531
35:40.654 --> 35:42.960
No, I've already ordered food to my condo.

532
35:43.571 --> 35:44.572
Thanks, though.

533
35:44.910 --> 35:45.911
Munin.

534
35:47.592 --> 35:48.700
Let's go have lunch.

535
35:50.520 --> 35:51.760
I'd like to treat you to a welcome lunch.

536
35:54.000 --> 35:55.001
I've got to go. Talk later.

537
35:55.854 --> 35:57.000
Hello? Mutta? Wait!

538
36:00.643 --> 36:01.644
Who the hell is Munin?

539
36:04.899 --> 36:05.900
- Whiskey? - Yes?

540
36:06.131 --> 36:09.032
Do you know who Mutta lives with at her condo?

541
36:10.595 --> 36:12.300
As far as I know, she lives alone.

542
36:12.376 --> 36:14.120
Why do you ask, Veekit? Is something wrong?

543
36:17.377 --> 36:18.578
No, it's nothing.

544
36:18.942 --> 36:22.200
I'm just worried there's no one to take care of her.

545
36:22.220 --> 36:23.760
Oh, I see.

546
36:26.283 --> 36:29.320
Do either of you know someone named Munin?

547
36:29.952 --> 36:30.953
Munin?

548
36:31.563 --> 36:34.440
Who's Munin? Mutta's never mentioned that name.

549
36:35.317 --> 36:36.318
Hong?

550
36:37.400 --> 36:38.700
Do you know who Munin is?

551
36:45.366 --> 36:46.367
Mun...

552
36:47.280 --> 36:48.281
Ta...

553
36:50.281 --> 36:53.082
I know gossiping is wrong.

554
36:54.910 --> 36:55.911
Hong.

555
36:56.911 --> 36:58.240
Save your mouth for eating.

556
37:01.459 --> 37:02.760
I am eating.

557
37:06.115 --> 37:07.300
And it's delicious.

558
37:12.208 --> 37:13.840
- Could we ask you a few questions? - Ma'am!

559
37:14.336 --> 37:17.700
Regarding the Tax Department Director-General's corruption scandal involving three billion baht,

560
37:17.744 --> 37:19.345
what progress has been made, ma'am?

561
37:19.700 --> 37:22.000
Our investigation has uncovered some facts.

562
37:22.040 --> 37:24.160
I'm taking steps to pursue legal action.

563
37:24.219 --> 37:26.440
Some say the Director-General might get away with it.

564
37:26.528 --> 37:28.040
Because he's one of your people, Nopnapha.

565
37:28.342 --> 37:29.776
What do you have to say about that?

566
37:30.278 --> 37:33.080
Anyone who says that clearly doesn't know me well enough.

567
37:34.689 --> 37:36.320
Throughout my political career,

568
37:36.952 --> 37:39.760
I've always upheld honesty and integrity. Everyone knows that.

569
37:41.700 --> 37:42.880
I don't want to hear such accusations again.

570
37:47.500 --> 37:51.520
Ma'am, someone sent us information about Hype Tech, the company that won the smart card project.

571
37:51.600 --> 37:53.640
They have a history of colluding to rig government bids.

572
37:53.701 --> 37:54.702
What?

573
37:54.875 --> 37:55.876
Who sent it?

574
37:56.198 --> 37:57.920
It was sent anonymously, with no source identified.

575
37:59.115 --> 38:00.480
Then double-check the information for me.

576
38:00.700 --> 38:04.300
If it's true, award the contract to the second-place bidder instead.

577
38:05.100 --> 38:08.301
There have been too many corruption scandals lately. We can't afford another one.

578
38:35.118 --> 38:36.119
Babe!

579
38:37.062 --> 38:39.440
Thank you so much. I really love you.

580
38:41.563 --> 38:43.080
I love you but…

581
38:44.672 --> 38:46.200
I've been feeling unhappy for a while.

582
38:47.787 --> 38:50.600
What's wrong? What's the matter?

583
38:51.046 --> 38:54.120
I care about you, Nina. I really do. It's just…

584
38:55.443 --> 38:57.400
I don't think our relationship is healthy anymore.

585
38:57.837 --> 38:58.838
Calm down.

586
38:59.406 --> 39:01.080
We can talk this through.

587
39:01.598 --> 39:04.480
I've just been a little busy lately.

588
39:04.515 --> 39:07.300
- But… - Honey, your coffee is getting cold.

589
39:07.916 --> 39:08.917
I'm coming.

590
39:13.160 --> 39:14.440
This is what I tried to tell you.

591
39:15.161 --> 39:16.162
Goodbye, Nina.

592
39:32.500 --> 39:33.501
[Jolene]

593
39:35.611 --> 39:38.760
Jolene, you won't believe what just happened to me.

594
39:39.430 --> 39:41.800
Hold on, Munin. Listen carefully.

595
39:41.872 --> 39:42.960
You're not going to believe this.

596
39:43.243 --> 39:46.170
Nopnapha called me in to sign the smart card project contract.

597
39:46.379 --> 39:47.820
Your plan worked.

598
39:47.840 --> 39:51.341
That company got kicked out, and we got the contract instead.

599
39:51.471 --> 39:55.120
We're about to take on a nationwide project.

600
39:57.216 --> 39:58.600
I've got to go.

601
40:21.024 --> 40:22.600
Drinks are on me tonight.

602
40:46.240 --> 40:48.241
[Veekit]

603
41:05.070 --> 41:06.071
Mutta.

604
41:06.275 --> 41:09.320
I brought you some rice porridge, congee, and fruit.

605
41:11.542 --> 41:12.543
Thank you.

606
41:13.830 --> 41:14.831
Still not feeling any better?

607
41:15.300 --> 41:16.880
Do you need any medicine? I can go get some.

608
41:17.611 --> 41:19.640
It's okay. I'm just feeling a little weak.

609
41:23.500 --> 41:24.501
Well, then...

610
41:25.301 --> 41:27.002
Make sure you eat, take your medicine, and get plenty of rest.

611
41:27.702 --> 41:30.100
And if you're still sick tomorrow, don't force yourself to go to work, okay?

612
41:35.976 --> 41:36.977
I'll get going, then.

613
41:40.357 --> 41:41.358
Veekit.

614
41:46.128 --> 41:47.376
Could you stay and keep me company for a while?

615
41:54.475 --> 41:55.476
Mutta.

616
41:59.027 --> 42:00.028
Mutta.

617
42:04.046 --> 42:05.047
Mutta.

618
42:07.247 --> 42:08.248
Why do you keep calling my name?

619
42:12.248 --> 42:13.249
Thank you.

620
42:19.008 --> 42:22.211
You know, I just realized I'd probably get stuck in traffic if I left now.

621
42:23.907 --> 42:24.908
Hey.

622
42:25.944 --> 42:27.445
Can you sit and talk with me for a bit?

623
42:38.118 --> 42:40.160
You can choose between rice soup and congee.

624
42:40.715 --> 42:42.520
Or we can split them both.

625
42:44.998 --> 42:46.600
I'll have the rice soup. You can have the congee.

626
42:50.032 --> 42:51.033
You said it!

627
42:59.694 --> 43:02.180
- How is it? Good? - Yeah.

628
43:14.187 --> 43:16.272
Wow, you must've been starving.

629
43:16.678 --> 43:18.400
Did you buy this for me or for yourself?

630
43:19.974 --> 43:21.120
For myself, obviously.

631
43:26.245 --> 43:27.246
I bought it for you.

632
43:28.702 --> 43:29.703
Really!

633
43:31.731 --> 43:33.760
I thought alpacas only ate grass and vegetables.

634
43:33.923 --> 43:35.040
But you eat everything, huh?

635
43:36.766 --> 43:40.120
Who says? There's pork in here too. See?

636
43:41.558 --> 43:42.800
Here, I'll eat this, too.

637
43:44.443 --> 43:46.000
Here, have some fruit.

638
43:51.259 --> 43:52.440
Now that's more like an alpaca.

639
43:53.670 --> 43:54.671
It's good, isn't it?

640
43:55.760 --> 43:56.761
It's okay.

641
43:58.240 --> 43:59.241
Just making sure it's not too hot.

642
44:12.840 --> 44:15.841
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

643
44:16.430 --> 44:19.300
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

644
44:22.027 --> 44:24.080
♪ Happy birthday, happy birthday...♪

645
44:25.118 --> 44:28.870
♪ Happy birthday to you ♪

646
44:37.400 --> 44:40.600
For your birthday this year, Daddy wishes you'll be a good girl,

647
44:40.816 --> 44:42.817
do well in school,

648
44:42.880 --> 44:45.881
and stop throwing tantrums.

649
44:46.128 --> 44:49.640
You're growing into a young lady. Keep this up, and all the boys will run away.

650
44:53.046 --> 44:56.800
Okay, my birthday wish for you, Titus, is that you'll listen to me and behave.

651
44:56.847 --> 44:58.840
And whenever you go somewhere, tell me first.

652
44:59.520 --> 45:01.040
Don't scare me like that again.

653
45:01.211 --> 45:02.320
And one more thing.

654
45:03.918 --> 45:06.120
No more screaming, okay?

655
45:06.622 --> 45:07.623
Okay!

656
45:08.120 --> 45:09.121
Good girl!

657
45:13.832 --> 45:15.040
Oh! The pretty sister is here!

658
45:15.574 --> 45:16.920
- See? - We just talked about this.

659
45:24.510 --> 45:25.511
Hey!

660
45:37.062 --> 45:38.063
Shit!

661
45:50.784 --> 45:54.120
If I really became your mom, which mom would you love more?

662
45:54.251 --> 45:57.121
Mom Nopnapha or Mom Mutta?

663
45:57.350 --> 45:59.320
I'd love Mom Mutta more, of course!

664
45:59.595 --> 46:01.960
And I'd quit being Mom Nopnapha's daughter, too!

665
46:02.043 --> 46:05.144
You should be happy that I get along with your daughter, Director.

666
46:05.414 --> 46:08.615
After all, I'm going to be her mother someday.

667
46:12.464 --> 46:14.480
When you watch other magicians perform,

668
46:14.998 --> 46:16.360
can you ever figure out their tricks?

669
46:16.412 --> 46:18.250
It's not just magicians I can see through.

670
46:18.475 --> 46:19.840
I can spot liars, too.

671
46:20.720 --> 46:23.320
So, to you, am I a magician

672
46:24.182 --> 46:25.183
or a liar?

673
46:29.243 --> 46:31.644
You filthy tramp! You cheap whore!

674
46:31.686 --> 46:33.140
Get the hell out of my house! Now!

675
46:33.270 --> 46:36.040
The reason he doesn't want to come home after work is that

676
46:36.297 --> 46:37.480
seeing your face is like seeing a ghost!

677
46:37.611 --> 46:39.680
You're the one who needs to get out!

678
46:40.780 --> 46:41.781
Come here!

679
46:41.814 --> 46:43.440
Die, you evil bitch!
